{
  "id": "primary-appraisal",
  "term": "primary appraisal",
  "definition": "Primary appraisal is the initial stage of evaluation in which a person interprets another person’s emotional cues and has an immediate emotional reaction to them. In the source context, employees responded to sad customers with other-focused feelings such as empathy or compassion, and to angry customers with reciprocal anger.",
